.SH NAME
ssoossh-nss - The ssoossh NSS daemon: directory users and groups for this host through systemd userdb.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh-nss [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
ssoossh-nss answers systemd's io.systemd.UserDatabase varlink interface on /run/systemd/userdb/com.github.mnestor.ssoossh, so nss-systemd resolves directory users and groups (getpwnam, getgrnam, initgroups) from ssoosshd over pinned HTTPS with a fleet key. It caches every answer, serves the cache while the server is unreachable, and never serves a name or id that /etc/passwd or /etc/group already has. With no subcommand it runs the daemon.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--admin-socket\fP="/run/ssoossh-nss/admin.sock"
	the admin socket the CLI and the daemon share

.PP
\fB--cache-file\fP="/var/lib/ssoossh-nss/cache.db"
	the persistent cache's SQLite file

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss.yaml"
	the daemon's configuration file

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ssoossh-nss

.PP
\fB--listen\fP=""
	bind the userdb socket at this path when not socket-activated (development and tests)

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="info"
	debug, info, warn or error

.PP
\fB--overrides\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss-overrides.yaml"
	the host override file


